  "statement": "Let $K_{m,n}^{(1,2)}$ be the $3$-uniform hypergraph on $V=V_1\\cup V_2$, with $|V_1|=m$ and $|V_2|=n$, whose edges satisfy $|e\\cap V_1|=1$ and $|e\\cap V_2|=2$. Let $L(K_{m,n}^{(1,2)})$ be its line graph, and let $a_i=(m-i)\\binom{n-2i}{2}$. Define\n\n$$\nd_i=\\frac{a_0-a_i}{i}.\n$$\n\n**Product-formula conjecture.** The number of successive vertex orderings satisfies\n\n$$\n\\sigma'(L(K_{m,n}^{(1,2)}))=m\\cdot\\prod_{i=1}^{m-1}\\frac{mn-\\binom{m+1}{2}+\\binom{i}{2}}{d_i},\n$$\n\nwhere each fraction is evaluated after disregarding all zero factors in both the numerator and denominator.\n\nThe paper presents this as a product formula complementing an earlier summation formula. Its status is not resolved in the supplied text.",
